                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_582">Whalley, Lancashire.
                        Cistercian abbey of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p><q>Iste liber procuratus
                           fuit monasterio de Whalleye per fratrem <persName>Willelmum de
                              Singleton</persName> quondam scolarem dicti loci quem quicumque a
                           dicta domo alienaverit anathema sit amen.</q> (front flyleaf, c. 1400).
                        Cancelled ex libris of Whalley abbey fol. 1v.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="#i" cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_4">Canterbury, Kent.
                        Benedictine cathedral priory of Holy Trinity or Christ
                        Church</orgName><p>Pledged in Oxford loan chests in 1455, 1457, 1465, 1473
                        (see further above). <q>Liber magistri <persName>Thome Dryffel</persName>d
                           qui debet dompno <persName>Roberto Estry</persName> monacho ecclesie
                           cristi Cant'</q> (fol. 1v). Dryffeld and Eastry (d. 1496), monk of Christ
                        Church (Greatrex, Register, 147), were both at Oxford in 1474–6 and it seems
                        possible that the book came to him as part payment of the debt. See Ker,
                        MMBL, ii, p. 269.</p></provenance>
